{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYY4FDudYPtfqs53Ys8c3b","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-236\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Add Subresource Integrity (SRI) hashes for all third-party CDN scripts\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Subresource Integrity (SRI) ensures that externally hosted scripts and stylesheets have not been tampered with by a CDN compromise or man-in-the-middle attack. SRI is an OWASP-recommended defence and complements the existing CSP. It is especially relevant for a hostel site handling enquiry forms and payment information.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"All third-party `<script src='...'>` and `<link rel='stylesheet' href='...'>` tags include `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes\",\r\n    \"SRI hashes use `sha384` or `sha512` algorithm\",\r\n    \"Browser console shows no SRI integrity failures in development or production\",\r\n    \"Process documented for updating hashes when third-party CDN resources change version\",\r\n    \"Google Fonts served via `next/font` (self-hosted) instead — eliminates SRI maintenance for font CDN\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Generate hashes: `openssl dgst -sha384 -binary resource.js | openssl base64 -A` or use srihash.com\",\r\n    \"Next.js `<Script>` component does not natively support `integrity` — use custom `<script>` in layout head for third-party scripts requiring SRI\",\r\n    \"Self-hosting fonts via `next/font` eliminates the Google Fonts CDN SRI maintenance burden entirely\",\r\n    \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Subresource_Integrity | https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Third_Party_Javascript_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"haiku\",\r\n  \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T08:34:26Z\"\r\n}\n[rerun: b1]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"6fd46a0e-3f27-42ca-8a09-3937f86c7e63","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:39:35.985Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-236\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Add Subresource Integrity (SRI) hashes for all third-party CDN scripts\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Subresource Integrity (SRI) ensures that externally hosted scripts and stylesheets have not been tampered with by a CDN compromise or man-in-the-middle attack. SRI is an OWASP-recommended defence and complements the existing CSP. It is especially relevant for a hostel site handling enquiry forms and payment information.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"All third-party `<script src='...'>` and `<link rel='stylesheet' href='...'>` tags include `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes\",\r\n    \"SRI hashes use `sha384` or `sha512` algorithm\",\r\n    \"Browser console shows no SRI integrity failures in development or production\",\r\n    \"Process documented for updating hashes when third-party CDN resources change version\",\r\n    \"Google Fonts served via `next/font` (self-hosted) instead — eliminates SRI maintenance for font CDN\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Generate hashes: `openssl dgst -sha384 -binary resource.js | openssl base64 -A` or use srihash.com\",\r\n    \"Next.js `<Script>` component does not natively support `integrity` — use custom `<script>` in layout head for third-party scripts requiring SRI\",\r\n    \"Self-hosting fonts via `next/font` eliminates the Google Fonts CDN SRI maintenance burden entirely\",\r\n    \"Reference: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Subresource_Integrity | https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Third_Party_Javascript_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"model\": \"haiku\",\r\n  \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-14T08:34:26Z\"\r\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Py5KaK8fdFeUwAMLustng1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Iteration US-216 (Attempt 2) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n2\t\n3\tCompleted: Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025 – Add safety reporting mechanism for user-submitted content (ID: US-216)\n4\t\n5\t### What was implemented\n6\t- **ReportContentButton.tsx** - Reusable React client component with:\n7\t  - Accessible report button (aria-label, title attribute)\n8\t  - Modal dialog for reporting harmful content\n9\t  - Pre-filled email (mailto:) link to safety@pelangicapsulehostel.com\n10\t  - Link to Safety Guidelines page within modal\n11\t  - Dark mode support with stone/red color scheme\n12\t- **Safety Guidelines page** (`/site/src/app/safety-guidelines/page.tsx`) - Comprehensive 320-line document including:\n13\t  - Definition of harmful content (8 categories: hate speech, violence, harassment, illegal activity, misinformation, explicit content, spam, personal information)\n14\t  - UGC scope clarification (hosted reviews vs. third-party platforms)\n15\t  - Report process with 5-step workflow (acknowledgment, investigation, decision, action, feedback)\n16\t  - 48-hour acknowledgment SLA and 5-10 business day review timeline\n17\t  - Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025 (Act 866) compliance details\n18\t  - Contact information (email, phone, address, hours)\n19\t  - JSON-LD WebPage schema for searchability\n20\t- **Terms & Conditions section 11** - Updated `terms/page.tsx` with:\n21\t  - User-Generated Content on Our Website subsection (hosted vs. third-party)\n22\t  - Safety Reporting & Content Moderation subsection\n23\t  - Links to Safety Guidelines page\n24\t  - Compliance statement for Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025\n25\t  - Renumbered existing sections 11-13 to 12-13\n26\t- **Reviews component integration** - Updated `Reviews.tsx` to:\n27\t  - Import and render ReportContentButton in each review card\n28\t  - Adjust card layout with flex-col and items-end for button alignment\n29\t  - Position \"Verified Guest\" badge and Report button side-by-side with flex gap\n30\t\n31\t### Patterns discovered\n32\t- Compliance pages benefit from clear section numbering and quick-access contact blocks\n33\t- Modal-based reporting UI reduces friction while keeping main content clean\n34\t- Clarifying hosted vs. third-party content scope prevents user confusion about where to report\n35\t- JSON-LD WebPage schema helps searchability of important compliance pages\n36\t- \"Verified Guest\" badge positions better when paired with action buttons in flex row\n37\t\n38\t### Acceptance criteria verification\n39\t- ✓ AC1: Report buttons visible adjacent to all hosted UGC (reviews in Reviews.tsx)\n40\t- ✓ AC2: Content Safety Guidelines page published with harmful content definitions and process\n41\t- ✓ AC3: Designated email contact (safety@pelangicapsulehostel.com) accessible within 2 clicks (button → modal → email)\n42\t- ✓ AC4: UGC scope documented in Terms section 11 (hosted reviews vs. third-party platforms)\n43\t- ✓ AC5: Online Safety Act 2025 compliance documented (both Safety Guidelines and Terms pages)\n44\t- ℹ AC5 (Legal): Legal review of CASP vs. ASP categorization is a non-technical business task\n45\t\n46\t### Gotchas\n47\t- Prior attempt timed out (exit code 124) before completion\n48\t- FAQSection build error (unrelated) was pre-existing in codebase — not caused by US-216\n49\t- Testimonials component exists but is unused; doesn't impact this story since it's not rendered\n50\t- Terms page renumbering required updating section headers 12 and 13\n51\t\n52\t### Test results\n53\t- All 4 files staged and committed successfully\n54\t- Diff size: 489 lines added, 9 deleted (well within budget)\n55\t- ReportContentButton: 78 lines, properly exported as default\n56\t- Safety Guidelines: 322 lines with complete schema\n57\t- TypeScript: Pre-existing config issues unrelated to new code\n58\t- Build: FAQSection error is pre-existing (unrelated to US-216)\n59\t\n60\t## Iteration US-173 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n61\t\n62\tCompleted: Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config (ID: US-173)\n63\t\n64\t### What was implemented\n65\t- Created `site/vercel.json` with Next.js framework configuration and environment variables:\n66\t  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT (default: \"book-now\") for local development fallback\n67\t  - EDGE_CONFIG placeholder for production Vercel Edge Config connection\n68\t- Verified complete A/B testing implementation already in place:\n69\t  - `flags.ts`: Flag types (CTAVariant with 3 options) and getVariant() function\n70\t  - `proxy.ts`: Server-side flag evaluation in Next.js 16 proxy (formerly middleware)\n71\t  - `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`: Reads variant from response headers (zero layout shift)\n72\t  - `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx`: GA4 custom dimension (dimension_1) records variant for statistical analysis\n73\t- Updated `.env.local` with NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT environment variable\n74\t- Verified build passes: all 68+ static pages generated successfully\n75\t\n76\t### Patterns discovered\n77\t- Next.js 16 uses `proxy()` function instead of middleware.ts (both cannot coexist in same project)\n78\t- `proxy.ts` already had A/B testing logic in place but vercel.json was missing\n79\t- Previous attempt failed with 12854-line oversized diff due to unrelated file modifications\n80\t- This iteration focused on minimal required configuration: vercel.json + env setup verification\n81\t- All acceptance criteria were already implemented by prior work; this iteration completes the story by adding the missing vercel.json configuration\n82\t\n83\t### Gotchas\n84\t- Vercel Flags UI in dashboard requires EDGE_CONFIG environment variable to be set in Vercel project settings\n85\t- .env.local should NOT be committed (already in .gitignore); only .env.local.example and vercel.json are version-controlled\n86\t- Next.js 16 proxy() is the evolution of middleware.ts; cannot have both files in src/ root\n87\t- Flag values must be evaluated server-side in proxy() or middleware to prevent client-side flicker\n88\t\n89\t## Iteration US-162 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n90\t\n91\tCompleted: Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup (ID: US-162)\n92\t\n93\t### What was implemented\n94\t- Created `lib/cache-utils.ts` with two functions:\n95\t  - `getCachedData()`: Generic utility that wraps fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\n96\t  - `getCachedRoomAvailability()`: Example implementation for room availability API calls\n97\t- Updated `Rooms.tsx` Server Component to import and demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\n98\t- Added try-catch error handling to gracefully handle AbortError when cache is invalidated\n99\t- No TypeScript errors; all 83 pages generated successfully during build\n100\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"f77375d1-63d5-4684-ab32-25a819680cd5","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:39:36.029Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\progress.txt","content":"## Iteration US-216 (Attempt 2) - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n\nCompleted: Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025 – Add safety reporting mechanism for user-submitted content (ID: US-216)\n\n### What was implemented\n- **ReportContentButton.tsx** - Reusable React client component with:\n  - Accessible report button (aria-label, title attribute)\n  - Modal dialog for reporting harmful content\n  - Pre-filled email (mailto:) link to safety@pelangicapsulehostel.com\n  - Link to Safety Guidelines page within modal\n  - Dark mode support with stone/red color scheme\n- **Safety Guidelines page** (`/site/src/app/safety-guidelines/page.tsx`) - Comprehensive 320-line document including:\n  - Definition of harmful content (8 categories: hate speech, violence, harassment, illegal activity, misinformation, explicit content, spam, personal information)\n  - UGC scope clarification (hosted reviews vs. third-party platforms)\n  - Report process with 5-step workflow (acknowledgment, investigation, decision, action, feedback)\n  - 48-hour acknowledgment SLA and 5-10 business day review timeline\n  - Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025 (Act 866) compliance details\n  - Contact information (email, phone, address, hours)\n  - JSON-LD WebPage schema for searchability\n- **Terms & Conditions section 11** - Updated `terms/page.tsx` with:\n  - User-Generated Content on Our Website subsection (hosted vs. third-party)\n  - Safety Reporting & Content Moderation subsection\n  - Links to Safety Guidelines page\n  - Compliance statement for Malaysia Online Safety Act 2025\n  - Renumbered existing sections 11-13 to 12-13\n- **Reviews component integration** - Updated `Reviews.tsx` to:\n  - Import and render ReportContentButton in each review card\n  - Adjust card layout with flex-col and items-end for button alignment\n  - Position \"Verified Guest\" badge and Report button side-by-side with flex gap\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- Compliance pages benefit from clear section numbering and quick-access contact blocks\n- Modal-based reporting UI reduces friction while keeping main content clean\n- Clarifying hosted vs. third-party content scope prevents user confusion about where to report\n- JSON-LD WebPage schema helps searchability of important compliance pages\n- \"Verified Guest\" badge positions better when paired with action buttons in flex row\n\n### Acceptance criteria verification\n- ✓ AC1: Report buttons visible adjacent to all hosted UGC (reviews in Reviews.tsx)\n- ✓ AC2: Content Safety Guidelines page published with harmful content definitions and process\n- ✓ AC3: Designated email contact (safety@pelangicapsulehostel.com) accessible within 2 clicks (button → modal → email)\n- ✓ AC4: UGC scope documented in Terms section 11 (hosted reviews vs. third-party platforms)\n- ✓ AC5: Online Safety Act 2025 compliance documented (both Safety Guidelines and Terms pages)\n- ℹ AC5 (Legal): Legal review of CASP vs. ASP categorization is a non-technical business task\n\n### Gotchas\n- Prior attempt timed out (exit code 124) before completion\n- FAQSection build error (unrelated) was pre-existing in codebase — not caused by US-216\n- Testimonials component exists but is unused; doesn't impact this story since it's not rendered\n- Terms page renumbering required updating section headers 12 and 13\n\n### Test results\n- All 4 files staged and committed successfully\n- Diff size: 489 lines added, 9 deleted (well within budget)\n- ReportContentButton: 78 lines, properly exported as default\n- Safety Guidelines: 322 lines with complete schema\n- TypeScript: Pre-existing config issues unrelated to new code\n- Build: FAQSection error is pre-existing (unrelated to US-216)\n\n## Iteration US-173 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n\nCompleted: Implement A/B testing with Vercel Feature Flags and Edge Config (ID: US-173)\n\n### What was implemented\n- Created `site/vercel.json` with Next.js framework configuration and environment variables:\n  - NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT (default: \"book-now\") for local development fallback\n  - EDGE_CONFIG placeholder for production Vercel Edge Config connection\n- Verified complete A/B testing implementation already in place:\n  - `flags.ts`: Flag types (CTAVariant with 3 options) and getVariant() function\n  - `proxy.ts`: Server-side flag evaluation in Next.js 16 proxy (formerly middleware)\n  - `site/src/app/book/page.tsx`: Reads variant from response headers (zero layout shift)\n  - `BookEcommerceTracker.tsx`: GA4 custom dimension (dimension_1) records variant for statistical analysis\n- Updated `.env.local` with NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_CTA_VARIANT environment variable\n- Verified build passes: all 68+ static pages generated successfully\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- Next.js 16 uses `proxy()` function instead of middleware.ts (both cannot coexist in same project)\n- `proxy.ts` already had A/B testing logic in place but vercel.json was missing\n- Previous attempt failed with 12854-line oversized diff due to unrelated file modifications\n- This iteration focused on minimal required configuration: vercel.json + env setup verification\n- All acceptance criteria were already implemented by prior work; this iteration completes the story by adding the missing vercel.json configuration\n\n### Gotchas\n- Vercel Flags UI in dashboard requires EDGE_CONFIG environment variable to be set in Vercel project settings\n- .env.local should NOT be committed (already in .gitignore); only .env.local.example and vercel.json are version-controlled\n- Next.js 16 proxy() is the evolution of middleware.ts; cannot have both files in src/ root\n- Flag values must be evaluated server-side in proxy() or middleware to prevent client-side flicker\n\n## Iteration US-162 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\n\nCompleted: Add React 19.2 cacheSignal() for Server Component fetch cleanup (ID: US-162)\n\n### What was implemented\n- Created `lib/cache-utils.ts` with two functions:\n  - `getCachedData()`: Generic utility that wraps fetch with cache() and cacheSignal()\n  - `getCachedRoomAvailability()`: Example implementation for room availability API calls\n- Updated `Rooms.tsx` Server Component to import and demonstrate cacheSignal() pattern\n- Added try-catch error handling to gracefully handle AbortError when cache is invalidated\n- No TypeScript errors; all 83 pages generated successfully during build\n","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1518}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WV7TevsTrmeqH9i6wC7s1t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have the story US-236 and some context from progress.txt. Now let me understand:\n\n**US-236 - Add Subresource Integrity (SRI) hashes for all third-party CDN scripts**\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n1. All third-party `<script src='...'>` and `<link rel='stylesheet' href='...'>` tags include `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes\n2. SRI hashes use `sha384` or `sha512` algorithm\n3. Browser console shows no SRI integrity failures in development or production\n4. Process documented for updating hashes when third-party CDN resources change version\n5. Google Fonts served via `next/font` (self-hosted) instead — eliminates SRI maintenance for font CDN\n\nLet me now check the current state of the codebase to find:\n1. Where third-party CDN scripts and stylesheets are currently loaded\n2. What third-party resources are being used\n3. How the layout/head is structured\n\nThis is a pelangi-website project (a Next.js application). I should look at:\n- The main layout file\n- The HTML head structure\n- Any _document.tsx or layout.tsx files\n- Google Fonts usage\n- Any other third-party scripts\n\nLet me explore the project structure first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2823,"cache_read_input_tokens":72196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2823},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"b3356192-727a-4250-87f3-92e95552e2b7"}
