{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011GN37Bc9G3kuh3QsnhuCU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture of all external scripts being loaded:\n\n## Summary of Third-Party CDN Resources\n\n1. **Google Analytics** (AnalyticsProvider.tsx):\n   - Script: https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={GA_ID}\n\n2. **Microsoft Clarity** (instrumentation-client.ts):\n   - Script: https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}\n\n3. **Facebook Pixel** (MetaPixelProvider.tsx):\n   - Script: https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js\n\n4. **TikTok Pixel** (TikTokPixelProvider.tsx):\n   - Script: https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js\n\n5. **Google Tag Manager** (via @next/third-parties/google in layout.tsx):\n   - Handled by Next.js's built-in solution, already secure\n\n6. **Turnstile CAPTCHA** (TurnstileWidget.tsx):\n   - Loaded via @marsidev/react-turnstile library (library handles the script loading)\n\n7. **Google Fonts** (layout.tsx):\n   - Already using `next/font/google` (self-hosted, no SRI needed per AC5)\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Add SRI hashes for all external scripts\n2. Ensure all scripts have `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes\n3. Document the process for updating hashes when versions change\n\nLet me create a plan before starting implementation.\n\n### Plan\n\n**Files to modify:**\n1. `site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx` - Add SRI hash to Google Analytics script\n2. `site/src/instrumentation-client.ts` - Add SRI hash to Microsoft Clarity script  \n3. `site/src/components/MetaPixelProvider.tsx` - Add SRI hash to Facebook Pixel script\n\n\n4. `site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx` - Add SRI hash to TikTok Pixel script\n\n**Files to create:**\n- `docs/SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md` - Documentation on how to update SRI hashes\n\n**Approach:**\nFor scripts loaded directly via `<script>` tags, I'll add integrity and crossorigin attributes. For dynamically constructed URLs (Clarity, Facebook, TikTok), I'll need to handle them differently—potentially by computing hashes at build time or documenting manual verification steps.\n\nThe real constraint is that Google Analytics uses a parameterized URL like `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA_ID}`, which means the hash would need to match Google's exact version and would require recomputation if they update the script. Dynamically created scripts via `createElement` can't use SRI at all, but static URL paths can. Looking at the actual implementations, AnalyticsProvider loads from a fixed path with only the ID parameter varying, while Clarity and others are fully dynamic in their construction.\n\nThe acceptance criteria specifically requires `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes on all third-party script and link tags. For Next.js's `<Script>` component, I can add these attributes directly. For scripts created dynamically through `createElement`, SRI simply isn't possible—that's a browser limitation. I need to either convert the dynamic scripts to use proper HTML tags with integrity attributes, or acknowledge that dynamic script injection can't meet this requirement.\n\nTo implement SRI, I'll need to fetch each script from its CDN, compute the SHA384 hash, and base64 encode it before adding it to the tags. This means downloading the actual content from Clarity, Facebook, and TikTok's endpoints and calculating the hashes for each one.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2625,"cache_creation_input_tokens":249,"cache_read_input_tokens":95058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":249},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"199e478a-3014-4f33-9844-d6ffed99de5e"}
