{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KnwnM4wgES2PYWc2upqqrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the stylesheets are locally imported via `./globals.css`, not from CDNs. The only external resource is:\n- Trip.com CDN for images (via DNS-prefetch) - not a script/stylesheet, so no SRI needed\n\nNow I have the complete picture. Let me create a detailed plan.\n\n## Implementation Plan for US-236\n\n### Files to Modify:\n1. **site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx** - Add SRI to Google Analytics script\n2. **site/src/instrumentation-client.ts** - Add SRI to Microsoft Clarity script\n3. **site/src/components/MetaPixelProvider.tsx** - Add SRI to Facebook Pixel script\n4. **site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx** - Add SRI to TikTok Pixel script\n\n### Files to Create:\n1. **docs/SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md** - Document process for updating hashes\n\n### Approach:\nFor scripts loaded via Next.js `<Script>` component with `src` attribute:\n- Add `integrity` and `crossOrigin` attributes\n\nFor scripts created dynamically via createElement and dangerouslySetInnerHTML:\n- Modify to add integrity and crossOrigin attributes to the created element\n\nFor Google Fonts (AC5):\n- Already using `next/font/google` which is self-hosted, no SRI needed\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Mapping:\n1. AC1: All third-party scripts have `integrity` and `crossorigin` ✓\n2. AC2: Use `sha384` or `sha512` hashes ✓\n3. AC3: No SRI failures in browser console ✓\n4. AC4: Document process for updating hashes ✓\n5. AC5: Google Fonts via next/font (already done) ✓\n\nLet me start implementing. First, I'll need to fetch the actual script content and calculate the hashes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4343,"cache_read_input_tokens":95307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4343},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"5ff67d67-a22b-4804-942e-7e05d76eb841"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KnwnM4wgES2PYWc2upqqrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\nThe pelangi-website Next.js application loads 4 third-party CDN scripts:\n1. Google Analytics: `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={GA_ID}`\n2. Microsoft Clarity: `https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}` (dynamic)\n3. Facebook Pixel: `https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js` (dynamic)\n4. TikTok Pixel: `https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js` (dynamic)\n\nGoogle Fonts already uses `next/font` (self-hosted), so no SRI needed.\n\n## Problem Identified\nThese scripts lack Subresource Integrity (SRI) protection against CDN compromise or MITM attacks. The acceptance criteria require:\n- All third-party scripts include `integrity` and `crossorigin` attributes\n- Use `sha384` or `sha512` hashes\n- No integrity failures in browser console\n- Documented process for updating hashes when versions change\n\n## Planned Changes\n1. **AnalyticsProvider.tsx** - Add SRI hash to Google Analytics script tag\n2. **instrumentation-client.ts** - Add SRI hash to dynamically-created Clarity script\n3. **MetaPixelProvider.tsx** - Add SRI hash to dynamically-created Facebook script\n4. **TikTokPixelProvider.tsx** - Add SRI hash to dynamically-created TikTok script\n5. **docs/SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md** - Create process documentation\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"docs/SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx\", \"site/src/instrumentation-client.ts\", \"site/src/components/MetaPixelProvider.tsx\", \"site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 120\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow I'll implement the SRI hashes. First, let me fetch the actual scripts to calculate accurate hashes:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4343,"cache_read_input_tokens":95307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4343},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"ad19fb22-cccb-4d79-b36b-ee00845f5909"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KnwnM4wgES2PYWc2upqqrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012T686oDqmMQfv9NkT4vKAD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"powershell -Command \"\n# Fetch Google Analytics script and calculate SHA384 hash\n\\$url = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-TEST'\ntry {\n  \\$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-TEST' -UseBasicParsing\n  \\$bytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes(\\$response.Content)\n  \\$hash = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA384]::Create().ComputeHash(\\$bytes)\n  \\$hashBase64 = [Convert]::ToBase64String(\\$hash)\n  Write-Host \\\"Google Analytics SHA384: sha384-\\$hashBase64\\\"\n} catch {\n  Write-Host 'Fetch failed: \\$_'\n}\n\"","description":"Calculate SHA384 hash for Google Analytics script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4343,"cache_read_input_tokens":95307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4343},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"8b2b56f3-e184-444a-a5ce-092959388371"}
