{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011o897nQz93TPuiokxjbwa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, this hash depends on the query parameter (id=G-TEST), which means different instances would have different hashes. That's not right. Let me fetch without the query parameter to get the base script, or with a specific ID. Actually, the query parameter shouldn't change the script content itself - it's just a parameter. Let me try fetching the actual script without the parameter to see if the URL works.\n\nActually, Google Analytics should return the same script regardless of the ID parameter. Let me verify this approach is correct by checking what srihash.com does for these scripts. But since I can't browse srihash.com directly, I'll need to use a different strategy.\n\nLooking at the problem differently: the hash should be calculated based on the actual script content returned by the server. For Google Analytics, the script content should be consistent regardless of the ID parameter. However, this can change when Google updates the script.\n\nLet me use a more practical approach:\n1. For Google Analytics, the hash depends on Google's current version - I should fetch without the parameter to get the current version\n2. For the other scripts (Clarity, Facebook, TikTok), they're dynamically constructed, so the hash will vary\n\nActually, I realize there's an issue with my approach. The Google Analytics script URL includes a dynamic parameter `?id={GA_ID}`, but the actual script content is the same. So the hash should be the same regardless of the ID parameter.\n\nLet me try a different approach: fetch the script from srihash.org or calculate it properly. But I don't have access to browsing that site.\n\nLet me reconsider the strategy:\n1. For scripts where the URL has query parameters, the hash should still be based on the script content\n2. Different versions of the script will have different hashes\n3. I should fetch the current version and calculate its hash\n4. When the script is updated, the hash needs to be updated\n\nLet me use openssl via bash to calculate the hash correctly. First, let me save the script content and hash it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1372,"cache_read_input_tokens":99650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1372},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"50ba8a86-c913-4e79-8acc-6cf8b0309d70"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011o897nQz93TPuiokxjbwa2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UYULvPVqj2FCHQstdPEBKY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"powershell -Command \"\n# Fetch scripts and calculate their SHA384 hashes in the proper format\n\\$scripts = @(\n    @{name='Google Analytics'; url='https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js'},\n    @{name='Facebook Pixel'; url='https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js'},\n    @{name='TikTok Pixel'; url='https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js'},\n    @{name='Microsoft Clarity'; url='https://www.clarity.ms/tag/test'}\n)\n\nforeach (\\$script in \\$scripts) {\n    try {\n        \\$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri \\$script.url -UseBasicParsing -MaximumRedirection 5\n        \\$bytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes(\\$response.Content)\n        \\$hash = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA384]::Create().ComputeHash(\\$bytes)\n        \\$hashBase64 = [Convert]::ToBase64String(\\$hash)\n        Write-Host \\\"\\$(\\$script.name)`nsha384-\\$hashBase64`n\\\"\n    } catch {\n        Write-Host \\\"\\$(\\$script.name) - Error: \\$(\\$_.Exception.Message)`n\\\"\n    }\n}\n\"","description":"Fetch and calculate SHA384 hashes for all third-party scripts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1372,"cache_read_input_tokens":99650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1372},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"93deeeb3-ce9d-40f2-912b-2200c75dfbeb"}
