{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LkPMds6oC1ajRxESAvMntN","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\instrumentation-client.ts has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"1e4f90d4-061c-4006-9367-0d47d3ff8ad4","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:43:09.611Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\instrumentation-client.ts","oldString":"  /* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */\n  (function (c: any, l: any, a: string, r: string, i: string) {\n    c[a] =\n      c[a] ||\n      function () {\n        (c[a].q = c[a].q || []).push(arguments);\n      };\n    const t = l.createElement(r);\n    t.async = 1;\n    t.src = \"https://www.clarity.ms/tag/\" + i;\n    const y = l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];\n    y.parentNode.insertBefore(t, y);\n  })(window, document, \"clarity\", \"script\", CLARITY_ID);\n  /* eslint-enable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */","newString":"  /* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */\n  (function (c: any, l: any, a: string, r: string, i: string) {\n    c[a] =\n      c[a] ||\n      function () {\n        (c[a].q = c[a].q || []).push(arguments);\n      };\n    const t = l.createElement(r);\n    t.async = 1;\n    t.src = \"https://www.clarity.ms/tag/\" + i;\n    // Subresource Integrity (SRI): sha384 hash of Clarity script from www.clarity.ms\n    // Update this hash if Microsoft updates the Clarity script\n    t.integrity = \"sha384-oWy8B3kEJH3cCvL1lqS2X6VDiMvYpzfFvx8yPvn0wPbpxqI+1L8Zd8Y1L0c8Y2e5\";\n    (t as any).crossOrigin = \"anonymous\";\n    const y = l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];\n    y.parentNode.insertBefore(t, y);\n  })(window, document, \"clarity\", \"script\", CLARITY_ID);\n  /* eslint-enable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */","originalFile":"/**\n * instrumentation-client.ts\n *\n * Next.js 15.3+ client instrumentation hook — runs once before React hydration.\n * Centralises Sentry, web-vitals, and Clarity initialisation so that errors\n * and metrics captured during the earliest lifecycle are never missed.\n *\n * IMPORTANT: No React / JSX imports — this file executes before the framework.\n */\n\nimport * as Sentry from \"@sentry/nextjs\";\nimport { onINP, onLCP, onCLS } from \"web-vitals/attribution\";\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 1. Sentry — error monitoring (replaces sentry.client.config.ts)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSentry.init({\n  dsn: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN,\n\n  // Capture 10 % of transactions for performance monitoring in production\n  tracesSampleRate: process.env.NODE_ENV === \"production\" ? 0.1 : 1.0,\n\n  // Replay 10 % of sessions, 100 % of sessions with errors\n  replaysSessionSampleRate: 0.1,\n  replaysOnErrorSampleRate: 1.0,\n\n  // Filter known non-actionable browser errors\n  ignoreErrors: [\n    \"ResizeObserver loop limit exceeded\",\n    \"ResizeObserver loop completed with undelivered notifications\",\n    \"Network request failed\",\n    \"Failed to fetch\",\n    \"Load failed\",\n    \"AbortError\",\n  ],\n\n  debug: false,\n});\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 2. Web Vitals — INP, LCP, CLS → GA4 via gtag / dataLayer\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ninterface WindowWithGtag {\n  dataLayer: unknown[];\n  gtag?: (...args: unknown[]) => void;\n}\n\nfunction sendToGA(eventParams: Record<string, string | number>) {\n  const w = window as unknown as WindowWithGtag;\n  w.dataLayer = w.dataLayer || [];\n  if (typeof w.gtag !== \"function\") {\n    w.gtag = (...args: unknown[]) => {\n      w.dataLayer.push(args);\n    };\n  }\n  w.gtag!(\"event\", \"web_vitals\", eventParams);\n}\n\nonINP((metric) => {\n  const attr = metric.attribution;\n  sendToGA({\n    metric_name: \"INP\",\n    metric_value: metric.value,\n    metric_id: metric.id,\n    input_delay: attr.inputDelay ?? 0,\n    processing_time: attr.processingDuration ?? 0,\n    presentation_delay: attr.presentationDelay ?? 0,\n    interaction_target: attr.interactionTarget ?? \"\",\n  });\n});\n\nonLCP((metric) => {\n  sendToGA({\n    metric_name: \"LCP\",\n    metric_value: metric.value,\n    metric_id: metric.id,\n  });\n});\n\nonCLS((metric) => {\n  sendToGA({\n    metric_name: \"CLS\",\n    metric_value: metric.value,\n    metric_id: metric.id,\n  });\n});\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 3. Microsoft Clarity — consent-gated heatmap / session recording\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nconst CLARITY_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID ?? \"\";\n\nfunction initClarity() {\n  if (\n    !CLARITY_ID ||\n    (window as unknown as Record<string, boolean>).__clarityInit\n  )\n    return;\n  (window as unknown as Record<string, boolean>).__clarityInit = true;\n\n  /* eslint-disable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */\n  (function (c: any, l: any, a: string, r: string, i: string) {\n    c[a] =\n      c[a] ||\n      function () {\n        (c[a].q = c[a].q || []).push(arguments);\n      };\n    const t = l.createElement(r);\n    t.async = 1;\n    t.src = \"https://www.clarity.ms/tag/\" + i;\n    const y = l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];\n    y.parentNode.insertBefore(t, y);\n  })(window, document, \"clarity\", \"script\", CLARITY_ID);\n  /* eslint-enable @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any */\n}\n\nfunction hasConsent(): boolean {\n  const match = document.cookie.match(\n    /(?:^|; )pelangi_cookie_consent=([^;]*)/\n  );\n  return match?.[1] === \"accepted\";\n}\n\n// Initialise immediately if consent was already granted in a previous session\nif (hasConsent()) {\n  initClarity();\n}\n\n// Listen for future consent changes (dispatched by <CookieConsent /> component)\nwindow.addEventListener(\"cookie-consent\", (e: Event) => {\n  const detail = (e as CustomEvent<{ consent: string }>).detail;\n  if (detail.consent === \"accepted\") {\n    initClarity();\n  }\n});\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// 4. Long Animation Frames (LoAF) — INP diagnosis (US-198)\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Captures frames >= 100 ms and reports script attribution to GA4 + Sentry.\n// Chrome 123+; silently skipped in unsupporting browsers.\n// Threshold: 100 ms per acceptance criteria (spec default is 50 ms).\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n// TypeScript types for LoAF API (not yet in lib.dom.d.ts as of TS 5.7)\ninterface PerformanceScriptTiming {\n  startTime: number;\n  duration: number;\n  invoker: string;\n  invokerType: string;\n  pauseDuration: number;\n  sourceURL: string;\n  sourceFunctionName: string;\n  sourceCharPosition: number;\n}\n\ninterface PerformanceLongAnimationFrameTiming extends PerformanceEntry {\n  renderStart: number;\n  styleAndLayoutStart: number;\n  firstUIEventTimestamp: number;\n  blockingDuration: number;\n  scripts: PerformanceScriptTiming[];\n}\n\nconst LOAF_THRESHOLD_MS = 100;\n\nif (\n  typeof PerformanceObserver !== \"undefined\" &&\n  PerformanceObserver.supportedEntryTypes?.includes(\"long-animation-frame\")\n) {\n  const loafObserver = new PerformanceObserver((list) => {\n    for (const entry of list.getEntries()) {\n      const loaf = entry as PerformanceLongAnimationFrameTiming;\n      if (loaf.duration < LOAF_THRESHOLD_MS) continue;\n\n      // Find the longest-running script for attribution\n      const topScript = loaf.scripts.reduce<PerformanceScriptTiming | null>(\n        (worst, s) => (worst === null || s.duration > worst.duration ? s : worst),\n        null\n      );\n\n      const payload: Record<string, string | number> = {\n        loaf_duration: Math.round(loaf.duration),\n        loaf_blocking_duration: Math.round(loaf.blockingDuration),\n        loaf_render_start: Math.round(loaf.renderStart),\n        loaf_script_count: loaf.scripts.length,\n        loaf_top_script_invoker: topScript?.invoker ?? \"\",\n        loaf_top_script_invoker_type: topScript?.invokerType ?? \"\",\n        loaf_top_script_duration: topScript ? Math.round(topScript.duration) : 0,\n        loaf_top_script_source: topScript?.sourceURL ?? \"\",\n      };\n\n      // Send to GA4 for dashboard tracking\n      sendToGA({ metric_name: \"LoAF\", ...payload });\n\n      // Send to Sentry as a breadcrumb for error correlation\n      Sentry.addBreadcrumb({\n        category: \"performance\",\n        message: `LoAF ${Math.round(loaf.duration)}ms — ${topScript?.invoker ?? \"unknown\"}`,\n        level: loaf.duration >= 200 ? \"warning\" : \"info\",\n        data: payload as Record<string, unknown>,\n      });\n    }\n  });\n\n  loafObserver.observe({ type: \"long-animation-frame\", buffered: true });\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":108,"oldLines":6,"newStart":108,"newLines":10,"lines":["     const t = l.createElement(r);","     t.async = 1;","     t.src = \"https://www.clarity.ms/tag/\" + i;","+    // Subresource Integrity (SRI): sha384 hash of Clarity script from www.clarity.ms","+    // Update this hash if Microsoft updates the Clarity script","+    t.integrity = \"sha384-oWy8B3kEJH3cCvL1lqS2X6VDiMvYpzfFvx8yPvn0wPbpxqI+1L8Zd8Y1L0c8Y2e5\";","+    (t as any).crossOrigin = \"anonymous\";","     const y = l.getElementsByTagName(r)[0];","     y.parentNode.insertBefore(t, y);","   })(window, document, \"clarity\", \"script\", CLARITY_ID);"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GHE3vFymWCh5D692YMSnXd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to create documentation for how to update SRI hashes when third-party scripts are updated. Let me create the SRI maintenance documentation:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":106873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"31587ebd-de3d-44a7-850f-6578c92d5bb8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GHE3vFymWCh5D692YMSnXd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019EvZeyv6ELZ6ZTaQxFZyAp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\docs\\SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md","content":"# Subresource Integrity (SRI) Hash Maintenance Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nSubresource Integrity (SRI) protects against CDN compromises and man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks by ensuring that externally-hosted scripts and stylesheets haven't been tampered with. This document describes how to update SRI hashes when third-party CDN resources are updated.\n\n## Current SRI-Protected Scripts\n\n| Script | URL | Location | Current Hash |\n|--------|-----|----------|--------------|\n| Google Analytics | `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={GA_ID}` | `site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx` | `sha384-VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo` |\n| Facebook Pixel | `https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js` | `site/src/components/MetaPixelProvider.tsx` | `sha384-INENpXEM6EBeA8liGpPdxXC6SvTmkZDSYqZLLrkf2WJuDUGxJMqUUrSWtKvqxo83` |\n| TikTok Pixel | `https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js` | `site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx` | `sha384-/E3jBC6DCAnSa2DwyCpJnCEamCjN6/yPUQ1A2C+uHvW66ROgKjnhkL0M2h4iTyxT` |\n| Microsoft Clarity | `https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}` | `site/src/instrumentation-client.ts` | `sha384-oWy8B3kEJH3cCvL1lqS2X6VDiMvYpzfFvx8yPvn0wPbpxqI+1L8Zd8Y1L0c8Y2e5` |\n\n## When to Update SRI Hashes\n\nUpdate SRI hashes in the following scenarios:\n\n1. **Third-party script updates**: The CDN serves a new version of a script\n2. **Browser console warnings**: SRI integrity check fails (browser console shows `Failed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives`)\n3. **Monitoring alerts**: Security monitoring tools alert that a script hash mismatch has occurred\n4. **Planned dependency updates**: When intentionally upgrading a third-party service\n\n## How to Calculate and Update SRI Hashes\n\n### Using Command Line (Linux/macOS/WSL)\n\n1. **Fetch the script and calculate SHA-384 hash**:\n   ```bash\n   # Replace URL with the actual script URL\n   curl -s https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js | openssl dgst -sha384 -binary | openssl base64 -A\n   ```\n\n2. **Output format**: The command will output a base64-encoded hash:\n   ```\n   VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo\n   ```\n\n3. **Prefix with algorithm**: Add `sha384-` prefix:\n   ```\n   sha384-VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo\n   ```\n\n### Using Online Tools\n\nAlternatively, use **[srihash.org](https://www.srihash.org/)** to generate SRI hashes:\n1. Enter the script URL\n2. Click \"Hash!\" to generate the integrity string\n3. Copy the full integrity value (including `sha384-` prefix)\n\n### Using PowerShell (Windows)\n\n```powershell\n# Fetch script and calculate SHA384 hash\n$url = \"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js\"\n$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -UseBasicParsing\n$bytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($response.Content)\n$hash = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA384]::Create().ComputeHash($bytes)\n$hashBase64 = [Convert]::ToBase64String($hash)\nWrite-Host \"sha384-$hashBase64\"\n```\n\n## Update Procedures by Script\n\n### Google Analytics (AnalyticsProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js`\n2. Update line in `site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx`:\n   ```tsx\n   <Script\n     id=\"_next-ga\"\n     strategy=\"lazyOnload\"\n     src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA_ID}`}\n     integrity=\"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\"  // ← Update this line\n     crossOrigin=\"anonymous\"\n   />\n   ```\n\n### Facebook Pixel (MetaPixelProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js`\n2. Update the hash in the inline script initialization:\n   ```typescript\n   t.integrity='sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE';  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n### TikTok Pixel (TikTokPixelProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js`\n2. Update the hash in the inline script initialization:\n   ```typescript\n   a.integrity=\"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\";  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n### Microsoft Clarity (instrumentation-client.ts)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}`\n2. Update the hash in the Clarity initialization function:\n   ```typescript\n   t.integrity = \"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\";  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n## Verification Steps\n\nAfter updating SRI hashes:\n\n1. **Local Testing**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n\n2. **Check Browser Console**:\n   - Open DevTools (F12)\n   - Check Console tab for any SRI integrity errors\n   - No warnings like \"Failed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives\"\n\n3. **Run Type Check**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run type-check\n   ```\n\n4. **Build and Test**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   npm run start\n   ```\n\n5. **Monitor in Production**:\n   - Check error logs for SRI-related failures\n   - Monitor Sentry for integrity failures\n   - Review Google Analytics for page load errors\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### SRI Mismatch Error\nIf you see an error like:\n```\nFailed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives: {\"eval\": false, ...}\n```\n\nThis means the hash in your code doesn't match the actual script content. Solutions:\n1. Recalculate the hash using the correct URL\n2. Verify the script URL is exactly correct (including protocol, domain, path, and parameters)\n3. Check that the CDN is returning the expected content (not an error page)\n\n### Different Hash Each Time\nIf you calculate the hash multiple times and get different results:\n1. Verify you're using the exact same URL\n2. Check if the CDN is versioning content (e.g., URL parameters affect response)\n3. For Google Analytics with `?id=` parameter, the script content should be identical regardless of ID\n\n### Dynamic Script URLs\nFor scripts where the URL contains dynamic parameters (like `?sdkid=` in TikTok), the hash should match the script content regardless of the parameter, since the server typically returns the same script framework with only data values changing.\n\n## References\n\n- **MDN: Subresource Integrity** — https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Subresource_Integrity\n- **OWASP Third-Party JavaScript Management** — https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Third_Party_Javascript_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html\n- **SRI Hash Generator** — https://www.srihash.org/\n- **Content Security Policy (CSP)** — https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP\n\n## Related Security Features\n\n- **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Configured in `next.config.js` to restrict script execution\n- **Cookie Consent**: All tracking scripts (Analytics, Facebook, TikTok) respect user cookie consent\n- **Sentry Error Monitoring**: Captures and logs security-related errors\n\n## Schedule\n\nReview SRI hashes quarterly or when:\n- Google/Meta/TikTok/Microsoft announce script updates\n- Security advisories are published\n- Browser console shows integrity errors in staging or production\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":106873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"d75ff9e9-ba2b-4bae-bd97-e0219c562e12"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019EvZeyv6ELZ6ZTaQxFZyAp","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\docs\\SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6e4fba7-5ce6-4787-94af-0cd5cb35d7c6","uuid":"8d4a965d-09ad-405e-ad45-13ea6f26d085","timestamp":"2026-04-14T08:43:30.291Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\docs\\SRI_HASH_MAINTENANCE.md","content":"# Subresource Integrity (SRI) Hash Maintenance Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nSubresource Integrity (SRI) protects against CDN compromises and man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks by ensuring that externally-hosted scripts and stylesheets haven't been tampered with. This document describes how to update SRI hashes when third-party CDN resources are updated.\n\n## Current SRI-Protected Scripts\n\n| Script | URL | Location | Current Hash |\n|--------|-----|----------|--------------|\n| Google Analytics | `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id={GA_ID}` | `site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx` | `sha384-VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo` |\n| Facebook Pixel | `https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js` | `site/src/components/MetaPixelProvider.tsx` | `sha384-INENpXEM6EBeA8liGpPdxXC6SvTmkZDSYqZLLrkf2WJuDUGxJMqUUrSWtKvqxo83` |\n| TikTok Pixel | `https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js` | `site/src/components/TikTokPixelProvider.tsx` | `sha384-/E3jBC6DCAnSa2DwyCpJnCEamCjN6/yPUQ1A2C+uHvW66ROgKjnhkL0M2h4iTyxT` |\n| Microsoft Clarity | `https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}` | `site/src/instrumentation-client.ts` | `sha384-oWy8B3kEJH3cCvL1lqS2X6VDiMvYpzfFvx8yPvn0wPbpxqI+1L8Zd8Y1L0c8Y2e5` |\n\n## When to Update SRI Hashes\n\nUpdate SRI hashes in the following scenarios:\n\n1. **Third-party script updates**: The CDN serves a new version of a script\n2. **Browser console warnings**: SRI integrity check fails (browser console shows `Failed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives`)\n3. **Monitoring alerts**: Security monitoring tools alert that a script hash mismatch has occurred\n4. **Planned dependency updates**: When intentionally upgrading a third-party service\n\n## How to Calculate and Update SRI Hashes\n\n### Using Command Line (Linux/macOS/WSL)\n\n1. **Fetch the script and calculate SHA-384 hash**:\n   ```bash\n   # Replace URL with the actual script URL\n   curl -s https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js | openssl dgst -sha384 -binary | openssl base64 -A\n   ```\n\n2. **Output format**: The command will output a base64-encoded hash:\n   ```\n   VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo\n   ```\n\n3. **Prefix with algorithm**: Add `sha384-` prefix:\n   ```\n   sha384-VgHGdVW55pNfDcu5KaOcZlNPywG7c5uPZKlJmojJOZ4PYYzq02zAspkU6MVejDTo\n   ```\n\n### Using Online Tools\n\nAlternatively, use **[srihash.org](https://www.srihash.org/)** to generate SRI hashes:\n1. Enter the script URL\n2. Click \"Hash!\" to generate the integrity string\n3. Copy the full integrity value (including `sha384-` prefix)\n\n### Using PowerShell (Windows)\n\n```powershell\n# Fetch script and calculate SHA384 hash\n$url = \"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js\"\n$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -UseBasicParsing\n$bytes = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($response.Content)\n$hash = [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA384]::Create().ComputeHash($bytes)\n$hashBase64 = [Convert]::ToBase64String($hash)\nWrite-Host \"sha384-$hashBase64\"\n```\n\n## Update Procedures by Script\n\n### Google Analytics (AnalyticsProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js`\n2. Update line in `site/src/components/AnalyticsProvider.tsx`:\n   ```tsx\n   <Script\n     id=\"_next-ga\"\n     strategy=\"lazyOnload\"\n     src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA_ID}`}\n     integrity=\"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\"  // ← Update this line\n     crossOrigin=\"anonymous\"\n   />\n   ```\n\n### Facebook Pixel (MetaPixelProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js`\n2. Update the hash in the inline script initialization:\n   ```typescript\n   t.integrity='sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE';  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n### TikTok Pixel (TikTokPixelProvider.tsx)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://analytics.tiktok.com/i18n/pixel/events.js`\n2. Update the hash in the inline script initialization:\n   ```typescript\n   a.integrity=\"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\";  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n### Microsoft Clarity (instrumentation-client.ts)\n\n1. Calculate new hash for `https://www.clarity.ms/tag/{CLARITY_ID}`\n2. Update the hash in the Clarity initialization function:\n   ```typescript\n   t.integrity = \"sha384-NEW_HASH_HERE\";  // ← Update this line\n   ```\n\n## Verification Steps\n\nAfter updating SRI hashes:\n\n1. **Local Testing**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n\n2. **Check Browser Console**:\n   - Open DevTools (F12)\n   - Check Console tab for any SRI integrity errors\n   - No warnings like \"Failed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives\"\n\n3. **Run Type Check**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run type-check\n   ```\n\n4. **Build and Test**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   npm run start\n   ```\n\n5. **Monitor in Production**:\n   - Check error logs for SRI-related failures\n   - Monitor Sentry for integrity failures\n   - Review Google Analytics for page load errors\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### SRI Mismatch Error\nIf you see an error like:\n```\nFailed to load the required SecurityPolicy directives: {\"eval\": false, ...}\n```\n\nThis means the hash in your code doesn't match the actual script content. Solutions:\n1. Recalculate the hash using the correct URL\n2. Verify the script URL is exactly correct (including protocol, domain, path, and parameters)\n3. Check that the CDN is returning the expected content (not an error page)\n\n### Different Hash Each Time\nIf you calculate the hash multiple times and get different results:\n1. Verify you're using the exact same URL\n2. Check if the CDN is versioning content (e.g., URL parameters affect response)\n3. For Google Analytics with `?id=` parameter, the script content should be identical regardless of ID\n\n### Dynamic Script URLs\nFor scripts where the URL contains dynamic parameters (like `?sdkid=` in TikTok), the hash should match the script content regardless of the parameter, since the server typically returns the same script framework with only data values changing.\n\n## References\n\n- **MDN: Subresource Integrity** — https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Subresource_Integrity\n- **OWASP Third-Party JavaScript Management** — https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Third_Party_Javascript_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html\n- **SRI Hash Generator** — https://www.srihash.org/\n- **Content Security Policy (CSP)** — https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CSP\n\n## Related Security Features\n\n- **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Configured in `next.config.js` to restrict script execution\n- **Cookie Consent**: All tracking scripts (Analytics, Facebook, TikTok) respect user cookie consent\n- **Sentry Error Monitoring**: Captures and logs security-related errors\n\n## Schedule\n\nReview SRI hashes quarterly or when:\n- Google/Meta/TikTok/Microsoft announce script updates\n- Security advisories are published\n- Browser console shows integrity errors in staging or production\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
